  ('class7-math-en-chunk-1-001', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch1', 'en', 1, 2, 6, 7, 1, 'Chapter One Rational and Irrational Numbers We perceive the diversity of this varied nature through numbers and calculations. In our previous classes we have learned about natural numbers, integers and fractions. These numbers are known as rational numbers. These numbers can be expressed as the ratio of two integers. Apart from these, there are numbers which can not be expressed as the ratio of two integers and those numbers are known as irrational numbers. In this chapter, we shall be acquinted with irrational numbers and discuss their applications. At the end of this chapter, the students will be able to— > Explain the square and square roots of a number; > Find the square root using factorization and division methods; > Solve real-life problems by applying different methods of finding square roots; > Identify rational and irrational numbers; > Locate the rational and irrational numbers in the number line. 1.1. Squares and square roots A square is a rectangle whose sides are equal. If the eee length of each side of a square is x unit, then the area of the square will be (x x x) square units or x? square units. | @ @ @ Conversely, if the area of a square is x” square units, then the length of each of its sides will be x units. eee In the figure, 9 marbles are arranged in a square array. The marbles are placed at equal distances with 3 marbles in each of 3 rows. So the total number of marbles is 3 x 3 = 3°= 9. Here, the number of marbles in a row and the number of rows are equal. Hence, the figure is a square. Therefore, the square of 3 is 9 and the square root of 9 is 3. .. A square is the product of a number Ix2=2R =4 multiplied by itself and that number (The square of 2 is 4) is the square root of the product. The square root of 4 is 2 Class-7, Mathematics, Forma-1 2 Mathematics 1.2 Perfect Square Observe the following table: or tee square a Area of the square (m’) 1 Ixl=1=1° 2 2x2=4=2° 3 3x3=9=3 5 5x5=25=5° 7 7x7 =49=7T a axa=a’ The characteristic of the numbers 1, 4, 9, 25, 49 is that they can be expressed as square of any other integer. 1, 4, 9, 25 and 49 are called perfect squares. The square root of a perfect square is a natural number. For example, the square of 21 is 21° or 441, which is a perfect square and square root of 441 is 21 which is a natural number. Generally, if a natural number m can be expressed as the square (n”) of another natural number 1, m is called a square number. This number m is known as a perfect square.', 470, '06-Mathematics.pdf', 'tesseract (pdftoppm -gray -r 200, -l eng)', 'OCR text; equations/stacked fractions/geometry symbols do not survive OCR reliably and are not quoted as exact. No confidence score produced by tesseract CLI in this run.'),
  ('class7-math-en-chunk-1-002', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch1', 'en', 2, 4, 7, 9, 2, 'natural number m can be expressed as the square (n”) of another natural number 1, m is called a square number. This number m is known as a perfect square. Properties of Square Numbers The square of numbers from 1 to 20 have been given in the following rows, Fill up the vacant boxes : Number| Sq. | Number} Sq. | Number} Sq. | Number} Sq. number number number number 1 1 6 36 11 121 16 256 2 4 7 12 17 289 3 9 8 64 13 169 18 324 4 9 81 14 196 19 361 5 25 10 15 20 Let us closely observe the unit digits of the square numbers listed in the table. We notice that the unit digit of these numbers is either 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, or 9. No square number ends with the digits 2, 3, 7, or 8. 2026 2026 Rational and Irrational Numbers 3 Activity 1. Will it be a square number if any number has any of the digits 0,1,4,5,6,9 in its unit place? 2. Which of the followings numbers are perfect square? 2062, 1057, 23453, 33333, 1068, 3969, 14161. 3. Write five numbers whose digits in the unit’s place help draw the conclusion that they are not square numbers. Let us take square numbers having 1 in the unit place from the table : Square number | Number 1 1 If the digit in units place is 81 9 either 1 or 9, the digit in 121 1 unit place of the square 361 19 number will be Pt Similarly Square number Number If the digit in units place 9 3 is either 3 or 7, the digit 49 7 in unit place of the 169 3 square number will be? and Square number | Number 16 4 If the digit in units place 36 6 is 4 or 6, the digit in unit 196 14 place of the square 256 16 number will be |? e Anumber whose rightmost digit, that is, the digit at the units place, is 2, 3, 7, or 8 is not a perfect square. e If odd number of zeros are in the right of a number, it will not be a perfect square. e Anumber may be a perfect square if the digit at its units place is 1, 4, 6, or 9. For example, 81, 64, 25, 36, 49 etc. are perfect squares. 4 Mathematics e Again, if even number of zeros are at the right of a number, the number may be a perfect square. For example, 100, 4900 etc. are perfect squares. Activity : 1. From the table construct a rule for square numbers whose digit in the units place is 4. 2. What is the digit in the units place of the following numbers: 1273, 1426, 13645, 9876474, 99580?', 474, '06-Mathematics.pdf', 'tesseract (pdftoppm -gray -r 200, -l eng)', 'OCR text; equations/stacked fractions/geometry symbols do not survive OCR reliably and are not quoted as exact. No confidence score produced by tesseract CLI in this run.'),
  ('class7-math-en-chunk-1-003', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch1', 'en', 4, 6, 9, 11, 3, 'rule for square numbers whose digit in the units place is 4. 2. What is the digit in the units place of the following numbers: 1273, 1426, 13645, 9876474, 99580? A table of a few perfect squares along with their square roots are given below : Sq. number | Sq. root | Sq. number Sq. root Sq. number | Sq. root 1 1 64 8 225 15 4 2 81 9 256 16 9 3 100 10 289 17 16 4 121 11 324 18 25 5 144 12 361 19 36 6 169 13 400 20 49 7 196 14 441 21 Symbol of Square Root To express a square root, J symbol is used. The square root of 25 is written as/25 . We know, 5x 5 = 25, so the square root of 25 is 5. Activity : Make a list of perfect squares from a few natural numbers. Finding the square root by prime factorization By resolving 16 into prime factors we get: 2116 16=2x2x2x2=(2x2)x (2x2) 218 Taking one factor out of every pair of factors, we get2x2=4 2 Square root of 16 = VJ16 =4 Again, by resolving 36 into prime factors, we get: 2026 2026 Rational and Irrational Numbers 5 36=2x2x3x3=(2 x2)x (3 x 3) 2 136 Taking one factor from each pair of factors, 2U8 _ 319 we get2x3=6 3 Square root of 36 = 136 =6. Observe : To determine the square root of a perfect square with the help of prime factors— At first, the given number is to be resolved into its prime factors. Each pair of the same factors must be written together, side by side. One factor is to be written from each pair of factors of same type, The successive multiplication of the obtained factors will be the required square root. Example 1. Find the square root of 3136. Solution : 2| 3136 2| 1568 2 |784 2 |392 2 1196 2 198 7 |49 7 Here, 3136 =2x2x2x2x2x2x7x7 =(2 x 2)x (2x 2)x(2x2)x (7x7) . Square root of 3136= 73136 = 2 x2x2x7=56 Activity : Determine the square root of 1024 & 1849 with the help of prime factors. 1.3 Determining the square root by division method An example illustrates the method for finding the square root of a number : Example 2. Determinine the square root of 2304 by division method. Solution : (1) Write down the number 2304: 23 04 (2) (3) (4) (5) (6) (7) (8) (9) Mathematics From right side, take two digits at a time and form 23 04 pair. Place a horizontal line over every pair. Draw a vertical line to the right of the number as in division. 93 04 | The first pair is 23. Its previous square number is 16, whose square root is ¥16 or 4. Write 4 at the right 3304 |4 side of vertical line. Now write 16 just below 23. 16 Now subtract 16 from 23. 23 04 !', 496, '06-Mathematics.pdf', 'tesseract (pdftoppm -gray -r 200, -l eng)', 'OCR text; equations/stacked fractions/geometry symbols do not survive OCR reliably and are not quoted as exact. No confidence score produced by tesseract CLI in this run.'),
  ('class7-math-en-chunk-1-004', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch1', 'en', 6, 8, 11, 13, 4, 'is ¥16 or 4. Write 4 at the right 3304 |4 side of vertical line. Now write 16 just below 23. 16 Now subtract 16 from 23. 23 04 ! 16 a Place the next pair 04 to the right of the remainder 7. Draw a vertical line (division symbol) to the left of 704. Put twice of the quotient 4 i.e. (4 x 2) or 8 to the left side of vertical line. Keep a space for inserting a digit in between 8 and the vertical line. Now, find an one digit number which is to be placed at the right of 8 so that the number so formed when multiplied by that digit equals to 704 or less than704. In this case it is 8. 88 |7 04 Put this 8 to the right of 4 in the quotient. The quotient obtained is 48. This is the required square root. *. V¥2304 = 48 N.B. while finding the square root using the division method, if the last digit of the number does not form a complete pair when grouping from the right, it should be considered without pairing. 2026 2026 Rational and Irrational Numbers 7 Example 3. Find the square root of 31684 by division method. Solution : 3 16 84 1 27 | the 189 348 | 2784 2784 0 .. Square root of 31684 = 431684 = 178 The required square root is 178. 178 Activity : 1. Determine the square root of 1444 and 10404 by division method. 2. Determine the digits at units place of the square root of the numbers 529, 3925, 5041 and 4489. Some important points on square number and square root e Ifa dot is placed on every alternate digit of a number, starting from the unit digit and moving left, the number of dots will be equal to the number of digits in its square root. For example, 81 = 9 (consists of one digit, here number of dot over the number is one since 81 = 81) 100 = 10 (consists of two digits, here number of dots over the number are two since 100 = 100) 47089 = 217 (consists of three digits, here number of dots over the number are three since 47089 = 47 0 89) Activity : Determine how many digits are in the square roots of the numbers: 3136, 1234321, and 52900. 8 Rational and Irrational Numbers Problems related to square numbers and square roots. Example 4. What is the least number which is to be subtracted from 8655 to get a perfect square number ? Solution : 8655 |93 81 183 555 5 49 6 Here, 6 is the remainder in finding the square root of 8655 by division. Therefore, if 6 is subtracted from the given number, then the number will be a perfect square. The required least number is 6. Example 5.', 482, '06-Mathematics.pdf', 'tesseract (pdftoppm -gray -r 200, -l eng)', 'OCR text; equations/stacked fractions/geometry symbols do not survive OCR reliably and are not quoted as exact. No confidence score produced by tesseract CLI in this run.'),
  ('class7-math-en-chunk-1-005', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch1', 'en', 8, 10, 13, 15, 5, 'root of 8655 by division. Therefore, if 6 is subtracted from the given number, then the number will be a perfect square. The required least number is 6. Example 5. What is the least number which is to be added to 651201 to get a perfect square number ? Solution : Here, the ramainder is 1565 in the process of finding the square root. So the given number is not a perfect square. A least number can be added to 651201 which makes the sum a perfect square and then its square root will be 806 + 1 = 807 Square of 807= (807)? = 807 x 807 = 651249. The required least number is 651249 — 651201 = 48. 2026 Mathematics 9 1.4 Exercise 1.1 Determine the square root of each by prime factorization: (a) 169 (b) 529 (c) 1521 (d) 11025 Determine the square root of each by division method: (a) 225 (b) 961 (c) 3969 (d) 10404 What is the least number which is to be multiplied with the following numbers to get a perfect square number ? (a) 147 (b) 384 (c) 1470 (d) 23805 What is the least number which is to be divided by the following number so that the quotient would be a perfect square ? (a) 972 (b) 4056 (c) 21952 What is the least number which is to be subtracted from 4639 so that the difference is a perfect square ? What is the least number to be added to 5605 so that the total sum is a perfect square ? Finding the square root of a decimal fraction The way in which the square root of the perfect square number or whole number is determined by long division, the square root of the decimal fraction is also determined in the same way. There are two parts of a decimal fraction. The part on the left side of decimal point is the whole or integral part and the part on the right side of decimal point is called decimal part. Rules for finding a square root In the whole number part, starting from the unit digit, a horizontal bar is placed over every pair of digits moving to the left. In the decimal part, horizontal bar is to be drawn over the digits in pairs from the right side of decimal point. If one digit remains at the end, a zero is added after it, and the bar is placed over two digits. In the standard process of finding the square root, a decimal point must be placed in the square root result just before bringing down the first pair of digits after the decimal point. Class-7, Mathematics, Forma-2 10 Rational and Irrational Numbers e For each pair of zeros in the decimal of a number, one zero is to be put after decimal point in the square root. Example 1. Determine the square root | Example 2.', 487, '06-Mathematics.pdf', 'tesseract (pdftoppm -gray -r 200, -l eng)', 'OCR text; equations/stacked fractions/geometry symbols do not survive OCR reliably and are not quoted as exact. No confidence score produced by tesseract CLI in this run.'),
