d at Tk. 90, what is the percentage of profit ? Solution: Here, the cost price of 15 ball pens is Tk. 75 and the selling price of 15 ball pens is Tk. 90 As the selling price is more than the cost price, it is profitable. Profit = selling price — cost price = Tk. 90 — Tk. 75 = Tk. 15 In Tk. 75 the profit is Tk. 15 » Ik. 1, 4, Tk. 1 75 1 20 » Tk.100,, ,, ,, Tk. «108 or Tk.', 499, '06-Mathematics.pdf', 'tesseract (pdftoppm -gray -r 200, -l eng)', 'OCR text; equations/stacked fractions/geometry symbols do not survive OCR reliably and are not quoted as exact. No confidence score produced by tesseract CLI in this run.'),
