  ('class7-math-en-chunk-2-009', 'class7-math-en', 'class7-math-en-ch2', 'en', 33, 35, 38, 40, 9, 'Tk. 1045 .. The cost price of 1 dozen of eggs = Tk. “= = Tk. 95 On an average the cost price of 1 dozen of eggs is Tk. 95 For profit of Tk. 3 for each dozen of eggs the selling price is or Tk. (95 + 3) or Tk. 98 .. If one dozen is sold at Tk. 98, the egg seller gets Tk. 3 as profit. Example 16. A goat is sold at a loss of 10%. If the selling price is Tk. 450 more, then it is 5% profitable. What is the cost price ? Solution : Suppose, the cost price of the goat is Tk. 100. With a 0% loss, the selling price is Tk. (100 — 10) = Tk. 90 With a 5% profit, the selling price Tk. (100 + 5) = Tk. 105 The selling price at 5% profit — the selling price at 10% loss = Tk. (105 — 90) or, Tk. 15 If the selling price is Tk. 15 more, the cost price is Tk. 100 ee TKD Tk, 108 15 30 a 4, yon os TK. 450, gyn gg Tk, 100% 450- ‘b 1 = Tk. 3,000 The cost price of the goat is Tk. 3000. Class-7, Mathematics, Forma-5 34 Proportion, Profit and Loss Example 17. Nabil bought 2 kgs of Sandesh at the rate of Tk. 250 per kg from a sweetshop. If the rate of VAT is Tk. 4 per Tk.100, how much did he pay to the shopkeeper ? Solution : The price of 1 kg Sandesh is Tk. 250 2” 2D 2 kg ” ” Tk. (250 x 2) =Tk. 500 VAT for Tk. 100 is Tk. 4 4 » ow» Tk , Tk. — 100 5 ow Tk.500,, Tk. 4X98 < TK 20 160 1 .. Nabil paid Tk. (500+ 20) = Tk. 520 to shopkeeper. Observation : Tax given at a fixed rate with the cost price of a thing is called VAT (Value Added Tax). Activity : 1, Going to a saree shop Kona bought a silk saree at Tk. 1,200 and a three piece at Tk. 1,800. If the rate of VAT is 4 percent, how many taka will she pay to the shopkeeper ? 2. Ishraq bought one dozen pencil at Tk. 250 from a stationery shop. If the rate of VAT is 4 percent, what is the price of each pencil ? Example 18. Monthly basic pay of Mr. Nasir is Tk. 27,650. The tax on annual income of Tk. 2,50,000 under the first slab is Tk. 0. If the tax on the